Proposal P0-3-verifier — migrate src/verify (human-owned, I-1) to the contract §7 Verifier, with I-4.

Justification. The build prompt's P0 task 3 asks for src/verify to implement the contract §7 `Verifier`
(stages(repo), run(candidate, repo, {upTo}) → VerifyResult). Because src/verify is human-owned, the agent cannot
edit it, so this patch is the change for the owner to review. It does three things. (1) In runCascade, a stage
with no detected command becomes `{ok:false, skipped:true}`. Today it is `{ok:true, skipped:true}`, and a repo
where every stage is skipped counts as "verified". That violates I-4 and the fail-closed principle (§1.7); after
the patch the aggregate passes only if at least one requested stage ran. (2) It adds src/verify/verifier.ts:
`CascadeVerifier` runs the `apply` stage first (contract §4) through the guarded applyEdits, then the cascade
cheapest-first up to `upTo`. It keeps verified edits and rolls back failed ones exactly. (3) It turns the agent's
temporary adapter (src/think/verify-adapter.ts) into a re-export, so callers switch to the human-owned code with
no other change. No verdict becomes weaker: every change makes a pass harder to get. Validated by the agent on
the commit this patch was generated from: `git apply --check` is clean, and typecheck plus the full test suite
are green, including the new test/verifier.test.ts.

Apply:   git apply proposals/P0-3-verifier.patch && npm run typecheck && npm test
Reject:  delete this file; the transitional adapter keeps P0 working.

